Llanelli businesses sell in town and, increasingly, to people who never visit the premises. A shop at Trostre, a maker in Burry Port, or a supplier in Cross Hands can take orders from Carmarthenshire, Swansea Bay and further afield if the website can show the products, take payment and tell the customer what happens next.

NC Digital designs and builds those stores. We are based in Merthyr Tydfil, not in Llanelli. There is no Llanelli office. The project is planned on calls and built remotely. You review the store before it goes live. An in-person meeting can be arranged when it is useful, but the work does not depend on us being on the premises.

## Prices for a Llanelli website

An online shop is the reason most people land on this page, and that work starts from £800. The other starting prices are here so you can see the difference:

- **One-page WordPress website:** from £199
- **Multi-page WordPress website:** from £600
- **Ecommerce website:** from £800
- **Pay-monthly website:** from £20 a month

All prices include VAT. The ecommerce price depends on the platform, how many products and categories you have, and whether you need bookings, subscriptions or a catalogue uploaded for you. It is not a one-page brochure with a buy button bolted on.

What is included at each level is set out in [how much web design costs in Cardiff](/blog/how-much-does-web-design-cost-in-cardiff/). Platform choices are on our [ecommerce development](/services/ecommerce-development/) page. If you sell across South Wales rather than only from Llanelli, see [ecommerce web design Cardiff](/ecommerce-web-design-cardiff/) and [ecommerce web design South Wales](/ecommerce-web-design-south-wales/).

## Who this is for around Llanelli

This page is for product and service businesses in and around Llanelli, not for a generic “Wales ecommerce” pitch.

- **Llanelli town, Felinfoel and Bynea** for shops and trades that already have local customers and want those customers to reorder online.
- **Trostre** for retailers who sell in person and need the same products available when the shop is shut.
- **Burry Port and Pembrey** along the coast, where visitors and residents search by place as well as by product.
- **Llangennech and Pontarddulais** towards Swansea, where delivery and click-and-collect both matter.
- **Kidwelly and Cross Hands** for businesses that sit between Llanelli and Carmarthen and do not want a store written as if it were in Swansea.

We only build the delivery and collection options you actually offer. If you deliver inside a set radius of Llanelli, the site should say that radius. If you post across the UK, the site should say that instead.

## Shopify, WooCommerce or SureCart

We use three platforms. The recommendation depends on what you sell, not on a preference for one town over another.

**Shopify** suits a Llanelli product business that wants the shop to be the website. The design is built around your products rather than a stock theme.

**WooCommerce** suits a business that wants the shop on WordPress, or that already has a WordPress site and wants to add products without moving everything. It is the usual route when you also want service pages alongside the catalogue.

**SureCart** suits digital products, subscriptions and service businesses that need to take payment without a large physical catalogue.

Whichever platform we use, you can edit products after launch. We set up the checkout, the payment gateway, product and category SEO, and Google Analytics before the store goes live.

## What every build includes

- Fully custom design — built around your brand, not a template
- Mobile-first layout for smartphone shoppers
- Secure checkout and payment gateway integration
- Easy product management — you're in control after launch
- On-page SEO for product and category pages
- Google Analytics and conversion tracking set up from day one

If you are not ready for a shop, a brochure site is a different project. [Web design in Llanelli](/web-design-llanelli/) starts from £199 for one page. [SEO Llanelli](/seo-llanelli/) and [logo design in Llanelli](/logo-design-llanelli/) are separate services. Nearby shop builds are [ecommerce web design Swansea](/ecommerce-web-design-swansea/), [ecommerce web design Carmarthen](/ecommerce-web-design-carmarthen/) and [ecommerce web design Ammanford](/ecommerce-web-design-ammanford/).

## Frequently asked questions

**How much does an online shop cost in Llanelli?**

Ecommerce websites start from £800, including VAT. A one-page WordPress website starts from £199, a multi-page WordPress website from £600, and a pay-monthly website from £20 a month, all including VAT. The shop price depends on the platform, the number of products and any extra features. See [how much web design costs in Cardiff](/blog/how-much-does-web-design-cost-in-cardiff/).

**Do you have an office in Llanelli?**

No. NC Digital is based in Merthyr Tydfil. Llanelli stores are scoped and built remotely, and you review the site before launch. We do not claim a Llanelli premises.

**Which platform should a Llanelli shop use?**

Shopify for a product store, WooCommerce for a shop on WordPress, and SureCart for digital products, subscriptions or service payments. We recommend one after hearing what you sell. The comparison is on our [ecommerce development](/services/ecommerce-development/) page.

**Can the store sell outside Llanelli?**

Yes, if that is how you fulfil orders. The site can offer local collection, a delivery radius, or UK-wide postage. We write the delivery rules you actually use, including Burry Port, Pontarddulais, Carmarthenshire and further afield when you serve those places.

**What if I only need a brochure website first?**

Start with [web design in Llanelli](/web-design-llanelli/). A one-page site is from £199 and a multi-page WordPress site is from £600, including VAT. A shop can be added later as its own project from £800.
